<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Afanasy Nikitin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">?–c. 1475</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Afanasy Nikitin was a merchant of Tver who travelled through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> between about 1466 and 1472, one of the first Europeans to describe the country. His travel notes, A Journey Beyond Three Seas, record life in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahmani-sultanate">Bahmani Sultanate</a>, where he stayed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bidar">Bidar</a>. He died near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smolensk">Smolensk</a> on his way home, around 1475.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/afanasy-nikitin.jpg" alt="Afanasy Nikitin" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alexxx1979 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tver._Monument_to_Afanasy_Nikitin_P7221267_2350.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
